+
+### JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)
+to a target JSON document and returns the merged document as a new value, without mutating `target`
+or `patch`. A `patch` object is merged into `target` member by member, recursively; a member whose
+patch value is `null` is removed; a `patch` that is not an object (including `null` itself) replaces
+`target` wholesale.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+const target = { title: 'Goodbye!', author: { name: 'Jane' }, tags: ['a', 'b'] };
+applyMergePatch(target, { author: { name: null, email: 'jane@example.com' }, tags: ['c'] });
+// { title: 'Goodbye!', author: { email: 'jane@example.com' }, tags: ['c'] }
+target; // unchanged
+```
